    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "9b48f16d887d549e306afb5533e9ee64675cbeb7",
            "parents": [
                "8946e2db2138e346034ad680f89653b9130c4523"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/75/77375/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "JunYe1993",
                "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                "username": "JunYe1993"
            },
            "createdOn": 1737515392,
            "author": {
                "name": "JunYe1993",
                "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                "username": "JunYe1993"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "These are supposed to represent hardware entities, not logical config entities.  I suspect most people would probably just put this info on the actual chassis."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Because Harma does not have direct access to the fan board FRU device, so it can only probe the configuration in a logical form."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How is the fan board detected?  If it is a separate entity, how do you know it is present?\n\nI think there is support being done elsewhere to add GPIO-based inventory detection.  We probably need to fix this once that code is available."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't an entry for the fan board.  That one is already up above.  This one appears to be a logical entity of type Chassis purely to hold configuration.\n\nAre you OK with that?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Good question.  I don't know what this is.  I thought maybe it was a second fan board, but that seems to not be the case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi Matt,\n\nIts role as a centralized coordinator for managing fan-related configurations or behavior that cannot be tied to a single hardware entity.\n\nTo avoid confusion, I renamed it to \"Fan Manager\", and make it clear that this is a logical construct and not hardware. I\u2019ve also added comments for it"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know what a \"logical construct\" means in entity-manager.  Entity-manager creates objects in `/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory`.  If you ask it to make a \"logical construct\" it is still going to populate this.  That means we end up with FRUs in external interfaces (like Redfish) that aren't actually FRUs.  Please move this into something that is a real physical entity.  Maybe the Harma board itself?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "To avoid redundancy, would it be acceptable to move the fan-related configuration to this harma_fanboard.json? Since the Harma board already has two sources, adding another configuration there feels unnecessary. The fan board is a physical entity, so it seems like the more appropriate place to handle this. so I would put it in Harma Fan Board 0 exposes section.\n\nWould this approach work?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If there is a real separate physical device called \"Harma Fan Board\", yes, that's fine to do.  We just need to ensure there is only 1 of them in the inventory model if there is only 1 physical device.  Do we have any way to detect it other than the \"Harma SCM\"?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 709,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "There is no GPIO present, so the only way to check whether the device is present or not is by using a weaker method\u2014sending an I2C command and checking for a response.\n\nThe probe condition is changed to Harma Chassis."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 710,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "This is still a new piece of inventory just to hold a fan config, which isn't necessary.\n\nIf I look for the term 'stepwise' in the yosemite4 files, I see it in 21 different ones, which implies that the fan parameters can be put with the inventory they represent.  If nothing else, this could all go in the Chassis object in the haram_mb.json file."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/harma_fanboard.json",
                    "line": 710,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "JunYe1993",
                        "email": "Daniel-Hsu@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "JunYe1993"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, move this fan table configuration into the Chassis object in harma_mb*.json."
                }
            ],
